AccountIn.description:
Another account of an app the team has: a sandbox, or a second org of the same system. On a plugin's
app it takes the first account's contract (the kind, whose account calls use, the OAuth app and the credentials);
on a custom app it signs in with the app's kind, with the kind's fields given in `credentials`.

get.description:
The app's accounts a call may name, each with what tells it apart: with `usable`, the team's live accounts
only, which a workflow step or an agent names; with `mine`, also the caller's own, which their chats name;
with `name`, the one so named (an empty list when none is), which the publish check reads.

post.description:
Internal (service token): agents-service calls it when it takes a thread over, so the new generation is
the fence before any write of the new owner, and a stalled old owner cannot write in between. Idempotent;
a lower generation than the fence is refused.
